+# Summary
+
+## Changed (`billing/invoice.py` only)
+- `Line.vat` now uses `net * rate` (it ignored quantity). PRICING.md rule 3.
+- `Invoice.add` raises `ValueError` for unknown rate names. Rule 3.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: 5 of 6 pass (was 4 failing). Three of the four failures are fixed by the changes above.
+
+## Still failing — needs your decision
+`tests/test_invoice.py::test_reduced_rate_small_item` expects VAT 0.02 on a 0.50 item at the reduced rate (5%). That is 0.025 exactly. Rule 4 of PRICING.md says half up, and gives "0.025 becomes 0.03" as its example. The code returns 0.03, so the test contradicts the finance-approved doc (it expects half-even/down). I left the test and the doc unchanged. The test likely needs correcting (VAT 0.03, gross 0.53), or finance needs to confirm the rule. Until then `python -m unittest` is not fully green.
+
+## Not verified
+Nothing beyond the unit tests. Rule 1 (`Decimal(str(value))`) is already implemented and I didn't change it.
